ted general construction scope. The weighted iteration and all-order homology are separately re-derived receiving arguments. Bibliographic identity: Identical Philip Engel manuscript title and arXiv2609.38442; compared source entry and exact current v1 original PDF. Only the separately recorded v1 loci are inherited. This is the same reading event, with no additional independent credit. Remark 8.3, rank-three real-torus quotient and hexagon/coarse-circle argument, lines 1684–1735. Scope: The exact proposed quotient extension was read. Paper III retains the literal-character obstruction and constructs its corrected map; this source reading does not endorse the rejected unmodified global quotient claim. Bibliographic identity: Identical Philip Engel manuscript title and arXiv2609.38442; compared source entry and exact current v1 original PDF. Only the separately recorded v1 loci are inherited. This is the same reading event, with no additional independent credit. Attached-source build: Lemma7.4 and complete proof pp18–19; cusp clause p19. Scope: Read the full finite-cap and cusp specialization lemma. The finite indices use the literal affine quotient presentation, intersection determinants and evenness; the cusp clause asserts its H2/H3 Mayer–Vietoris computation in one sentence. The current iv:rank\_two\_specialization proof supplies its complete integral matrices, actual unit-preserving family map and primitive cross-line construction. No omitted computation is represented as printed in Engel. PDF SHA256 c9c17426430e44582dfe3fceca5b1486174d5181396a14be43a6a960f4f514a0 Same identified author/title/arXiv work or original edition; current verification applies only to the exact opened edition and locators stated here. Bibliographic identity: Identical Philip Engel manuscript title and arXiv2609.38442; compared source entry and exact current v1 original PDF. Only the separately recorded v1 loci are inherited. This is the same reading event, with no additional independent